{
  "about": "The picture viewer's zoom (docs/specs/media.md 5). `frames`: a picture of `own` pixels fitted into a `room` of points with `margin` clear on each side, shrunk to fit and never grown; `own_scale` is the scale of its own size (a picture pixel a point), `max_scale` the furthest zoom and `detail_scale` where a press on a fitted picture goes. `moves`: a view (`scale` in times the fitted size, `x` and `y` the picture's centre from the room's, in points) and what a move makes of it; a point (`at`) is from the room's centre too. `wheel`: what one wheel event multiplies the scale by, `delta` the points it would scroll a page, positive down, `pinch` a trackpad's pinch arriving as a wheel with Control held. Numbers agree to a thousandth. Every client agrees on every case (lumia_core::viewer).",
